in reality there's no average when it  comes to abortions each person has their  own reasons circumstances life this  video is based in facts and statistics  to give a general look at who when and  why people have abortions the majority  of women receiving abortions are not  teenagers she's most likely a mother  with almost 60% of those seeking an  abortion already having given birth and  she most likely belongs to an organized  religion common reasons cited for  abortions include financial concerns and  the pregnancies interference with work  school and other responsibilities  according to 2005 research data from  2013 shows that a majority of abortions  happen in the first eight weeks of  pregnancy at that time the embryo is  approximately as large as a pencil  eraser and although very small and has a  beating heart by six weeks research from  the Royal College of Obstetricians and  Gynaecologists reported in 2010 that  before 24 weeks a fetus cannot feel pain  vacuum aspiration is the most common  method of in clinic abortions the  procedures performed by opening the  cervix wide enough to be able to use  suction to remove the pregnancy the  suction part lasts about one minute and  does not involve any incisions or cuts  it is not risk-free and there can be  bleeding and cramping afterward but  complications are rare and a 2014 study  conducted by the University of  California San Francisco minor  complications arose and less than 2% of  the abortions and major complications  happen very rarely there are more  complications at a higher risk of death  bringing a baby to term and giving birth  according to 2012 research after an  abortion it is normal to feel a range of  emotions but according to a study of  women who have had an abortion  the vast majority deemed at the right  decision and a study published in 2016  found that the risk of mental health  problems is no greater for women who  have had an abortion then for women who  have given birth after attempting to  obtain an abortion knowing these facts  will hopefully help change the way we  talk about abortions and the media with  our friends and family and with those  who have a different perspective  [Music]
 

